Name: amd-video-enhancer
Version: @RPM_VERSION@
Release: @RPM_RELEASE@
Summary: Linux-first AMD GPU video enhancement application
License: MIT
URL: https://github.com/Rolaand-Jayz/AMD-V.E.-
BuildArch: x86_64
Source1: @RPM_FILELIST_NAME@
AutoReqProv: no
Requires: /usr/bin/bash

%description
Linux-first AMD GPU video enhancement package built from the canonical staged release root.

The app and bundled userspace dependencies remain private under
/opt/amd-video-enhancer, with only thin entrypoints exposed under /usr/bin.

Arch Linux on Ryzen 7 7800X3D + Radeon RX 7900 GRE remains the primary verified stack.
Other distro packages are published as preview builds and should be validated on the target system.

%prep

%build

%install
mkdir -p %{buildroot}
cp -a %{staged_root}/. %{buildroot}/

%files -f %{SOURCE1}

%changelog
* @RPM_CHANGELOG_DATE@ @PACKAGE_MAINTAINER@ - @RPM_VERSION@-@RPM_RELEASE@
- Release packaging refresh with MIT licensing and checksum publication
